WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-Welcome back to "Late Night"!

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.534
We're here with Amber Ruffin
and Lacey Lamar.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:04.734
They're sisters.
They're wonderful.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.200
Amber works for this show.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.634
Amber, you also have your own
show, "The Amber Ruffin Show."

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.501
You recently had --
I mean, I guess,

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:13.300
a hero of both of yours.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.234
Is hero the right word
for El DeBarge?

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:19.767
-Hero, husband...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:20.901
-Idol.
-Idol.

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.067
-Hey, jinx!
-Jinx.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.067
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.467
-So there you are.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.501
So, Lacey, you're on the show.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.801
There's El DeBarge there.
There you are, Lacey.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.367
Were you -- Could you be in the
moment, or was it all a blur?

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.501
-No, I don't remember anything.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:36.701
I think I was hovering over my
body, watching that happen.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.133
I don't know what I said.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.834
-Did El DeBarge enjoy his time,

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.968
or did he feel maybe
like a little stalked?

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:46.267
-I was terrified
he would have a bad time,

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.868
so I talked to him
as little as possible.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.367
I was scared!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.534
-I did not.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.100
We hung out and became friends.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.267
[ Laughter ]
-They did, they did.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:57.334
-It should be noted,
El DeBarge has been very

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.000
taken care of you guys.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.133
This was the first dedication
of your first book.

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:02.601
-Yeah.
-"This book is dedicated

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.901
to Black mothers and fathers,
like James and Theresa Ruffin,

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.367
who teach us how to deal
with racism,

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.834
to Black brothers and sisters

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.634
like Chrystal, Angela,
and Jimmy,

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.834
who provide support,
and Black children like Amani

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.400
who hopefully have it easier
than we did.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.267
And most of all, this book
is dedicated to El DeBarge.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.834
You are truly
the Rhythm of the Night."

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.367
-He is.
-And then...

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:30.601
-I love him.
-...I want to note

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.868
you had a chance, obviously,
to have a second dedication

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.567
to maybe cover
more people in your life.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.067
-Yeah.
-Throw a wider net.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:40.367
"This book is dedicated
to all white people everywhere.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.400
Just kidding.
The opposite of that."

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.567
"This book is dedicated
to our family and friends

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.934
who experienced
all these stories with us.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.467
Just kidding.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:53.734
This book
is dedicated to El DeBarge."

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:56.801
-It is.
-It is.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.234
-It is.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.133
Some would say everything we do
is dedicated to him.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.534
-I know you're a talented
writer, Lacey.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.534
I did not realize the -- the --

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.267
the depths
of your artistic talent.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.868
-I know
what you're about to show,

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.367
and that was my fourth grade...
-Fourth grade?

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:12.567
-...art project, yes.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:13.901
-This was your fourth grade
art project?

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.200
[ Laughter ]
-And you know that's good.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.467
-That is good.
-Isn't it great?

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:21.100
[ Applause ]

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.968
-You guys --
-But wait, wait.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.200
It's on my mantel right now.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.801
-It's on her mantel right now!
-You framed it?

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.734
-No.
It's just hanging there.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.801
-It's just hanging there.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.167
-Is it just, like, a loose piece
of fourth-grade paper?

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.834
-Oh, it's on a board.
-It's on a board --

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.467
it's on a canvas.
-Oh, it's on a canvas.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:39.100
-It's pencil on canvas, Seth.
-Oh, pencil on canvas.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.934
-[ Laughs ] El DeBarge
is looking everywhere.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.934
-I'm waiting for it to come up
at auction at Christie's.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:46.801
-Listen, I'm not selling that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.000
-Hey, you're doing the countdown

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.868
to the Macy's Thanksgiving Day
Parade, Amber.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.667
-Yay!
-On Wednesday.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.601
-I love
the Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.300
-You have always loved --
you love a --

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.968
I mean, I know this sounds
like a song in a musical.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:03.801
You love a parade.
-♪ I love a parade ♪

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.567
I super do.

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:09.033
Sometimes I forget
what holiday it is.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:12.133
The parade comes out our window
at work, and we can watch it.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.033
-Yeah.
-And I used to watch it

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:16.367
like this out of our window,
you know, because we look over

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:18.000
Rockefeller Center
and the tree and stuff.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.567
And I would watch the parade
like this,

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:22.934
and Michelle Wolf would be
two desks down talking about,

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:26.300
"I hate parades!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.701
-Where do you come out
on parades?

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.300
-I love a parade.
-You love a parade, too.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.300
-It's amazing.
-It's so prancy.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.601
-Yeah, I do.
I love a parade.

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:38.467
I worked one time
at a retirement home,

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:39.934
and I wasn't the only person
that did this,

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:42.968
but we actually were counting
our residents that we had.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.868
And we had seven,
and I kept counting seven.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.868
And then, one time I looked,
and we counted six.

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.634
And Charlene went by on a horse.

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:51.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.534
I don't know why I shared that.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.601
But I do love parades.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:56.801
-That should've been
in the book!

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.133
-Is it exciting when you see
the book on a shelf?

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.100
Do you like going to a bookstore
and seeing the Ruffin girls?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.133
-We love it.
-The book's on the shelf

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.200
downstairs, Seth,
in this very building.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.767
-Is it really?
-Yes.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.667
-It is.
-Not the new one, sorry.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.467
[ Laughter ]
I'm sorry I said that.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.467
-But if people
don't have the old one --

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.868
-The old one is downstairs.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.634
-And that is very cute to pass

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:23.334
when you go
into your job every day.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.133
-Now, you had El DeBarge on
"The Amber Ruffin Show"

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.501
this year.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:30.467
You've had some other real
sort of bucket-list guests.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:32.267
-First of all,
we had El DeBarge on,

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:35.200
and we played a game with him
called "Know Your El DeBarge,"

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.534
and we beat him.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:38.167
-What do you mean "we"?

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.033
I won.
-Lacey won. Lacey did win.

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.133
-Did he get any El DeBarge
questions right?

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.567
-Yeah. Like, he knew
where he was born, but...

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.400
-He didn't know enough.
-No.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.534
We had Babyface on,
and he played a game called

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:58.200
"Name That Ooh," where I "oohed"
oohs and aahs from songs

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.634
he wrote, and he had to guess --

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:03.934
[ Laughter ] --
what song it was from.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.067
-How did he do?

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:08.234
-He was, um, disappointed...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:11.400
...in my ability
to convey the music.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.300
-Gotcha.
He put it on you.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.200
-Yeah.
He wasn't wrong.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.601
-All right.
That's very kind of you

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:20.267
to not blame it on Babyface,
yeah.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.000
It is always so lovely
to have you guys.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.934
Thank you for being here with us
on this week of family.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:27.467
I know you guys are family, but
you're also family to this show,

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:29.200
and it is so lovely to be here
together with you guys.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.200
Congratulations.
Two books!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:35.200
Two books and an art --
and a masterpiece.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:39.234
Amber Ruffin and Lacey Lamar,
everybody.

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:41.567
"The World Record Book
of Racist Stories"

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.868
is available now
wherever you buy your books.

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:46.434
Please support local
and independent bookstores.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.968
We'll be right back with more
"Late Night."

